From 2c824b16c711ef0e58533a5a65e0ff1cf7d4ef2b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 18:04:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: rockchip: i2s: Register the PCM before the DAI

A card that was registered before its CPU DAI is retried by
snd_soc_add_component() as soon as any component is added. The DAI
component satisfies the DAI link's platform, which defaults to the CPU
of_node, so the card can bind right after the DAI is registered and
before the dmaengine PCM component of the same device exists. The card
then has no PCM component and every open of the PCM fails with -EINVAL.

Register the dmaengine PCM first, as rockchip_spdif already does.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_i2s.c | 10 +++++-----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_i2s.c b/sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_i2s.c
index 261f36d4c2fd..cfdb982b53c2 100644
--- a/sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_i2s.c
+++ b/sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_i2s.c
@@ -827,14 +827,14 @@ static int rockchip_i2s_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	ret = devm_snd_soc_register_component(&pdev->dev,
-					      &rockchip_i2s_component,
-					      dai, 1);
-
+	/* Register the PCM first, a card can bind as soon as the DAI is added */
+	ret = devm_snd_dmaengine_pcm_register(&pdev->dev, NULL, 0);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	ret = devm_snd_dmaengine_pcm_register(&pdev->dev, NULL, 0);
+	ret = devm_snd_soc_register_component(&pdev->dev,
+					      &rockchip_i2s_component,
+					      dai, 1);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
